y the next one revealed.\\n\\n## The pattern — fourth consumer break from one change\\n\\n| Issue | Producer change | Stale consumer |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| #1863 | #1837 renamed the per-plugin block comment to an ordinal | `prepare-flow-b-fixture.ts` literal |\\n| #1870 | #1837 replaced a duplicate-tolerant check with a uniqueness requirement | `Mode: 'Auto'` emits two attachments |\\n| #1877 | #1864 renamed the worker startup log line | `wait-for-workers-runtime.ts` markers |\\n| **this** | **#1837 renamed app identifiers to positional** | fixture apps generated in isolation collide with the host's |\\n\\nThe first three coupled on **strings**; this one couples on **generated identifier namespace**, which\\nis worse — it produces a module that does not parse rather than a check that does not match.\\n\\n## Bounded fix\\n\\nMake the injected fixture blocks use identifiers that cannot collide with the host module. Either\\nrewrite the sliced block's `app_\\u003cn\\u003e` identifiers (including `_workdir`/`_otel` suffixed ones) to a\\nfixture-specific namespace, or generate the fixture apps at an index offset past the host's app count.\\nRenaming is preferable: an offset silently breaks again if the host's app count changes between\\ngeneration and injection.\\n\\nOut of scope: do not change the apps generator's positional naming — it is behaving as #1837 intends,\\nand other consumers now depend on it.\\n\\n## Definition of Done\\n\\n- [ ] Injecting the readiness fixture into a project that already declares `app_0` produces no duplicate `const` declaration, proven by a test over **real generator output** rather than a hand-written string.\\n- [ ] Every identifier in the injected block is renamed consistently, including `_workdir` and any other suffixed references.\\n- [ ] A test proves the emitted module parses after injection (e.g. type-check or parse the result), not merely that the text differs.\\n- [ ] `listener-fault-controller` starts and binds 18999, and `runtime.health.listener-unreachable` passes in both hosted tiers.\\n- [ ] No change to `generate-register-apps.ts`; `deno.lock` unchanged.\\n\",\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"fix(e2e): readiness-fixture app injection collides with the project's positional app identifiers, so listener-fault-controller never starts\"}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
