ame: ..., port? ...})` fine.\n\nHealthCheckPath: app type default → `withHttpHealthCheck({ path: ..., endpointName: 'http' })` — stub exists.\n\nVITE injection with ServiceReferences: uses `buildViteEnvVarName(ref)` and `getResourceEndpoint(_services.get(ref), 'http')` — both available. And `vite.full`/`vite.shorthand` — stub returns { full, shorthand }. \n\nAlso `_infrastructure.primaryCacheWiring` for RequiresKv — `_infrastructure` param typed InfrastructureContext with `primaryCacheWiring?: unknown` — stub register-infrastructure.mts exports that interface. withCacheReference stubbed. I'll give worker RequiresKv: true to exercise that path — fixture apps have RequiresKv: false so fixture blocks don't use it; host does. Fine.\n\nNow writing deno check invocation from within the probe: use `new Deno.Command(Deno.execPath(), { args: ['check', '--no-config', path], stdout: 'piped', stderr: 'piped' })` same as committed test.\n\nOne catch: `deno check --no-config` on a module importing `../.aspire/modules/aspire.mts` and `./_aspire-compat.mts` — the committed test writes those stubs. My probe replicates. \n\nAlso: probe needs `--allow-read --allow-write --allow-run --allow-env`? deno.Command needs --allow-run. TempDir needs --allow-write. Fine — I'll run `deno run --allow-all`.\n\nThe import path from probe location `.llm/tmp/eval-1898-f2/` to worktree packages: `../../packages/cli/...`. \n\nHmm wait — will the injector import chain hit `listener-fault-controller.ts` and `listener-readiness-gates.ts` — all relative within e2e tree; and `template-registry.ts` from `../../../../../../src/kernel/application/registries/template-registry.ts` — relative; and extension-axes domain — relative. None of these import bare npm/jsr? `template-registry.ts` might. Whatever — resolution via workspace import map handles `@netscript/*` and `@std/*`. deno run without --config: the workspace discovery finds root deno.json automatically since the imported files are inside the workspace dir tree. Should work. Let me write it.\n\nAlso — one more F6 subtlety to probe: re-injecting the RAW injected output (not the single-quote variant). The committed test uses withSingleQuotedAppNames(injected) — I'll test raw too.\n\nAnd an extra adversarial probe: what if the host module contains a STRING containing `app_0` (e.g., app named \"app_0-ish\")? Rename only touches fixture blocks — safe.\n\nAnd the reverse-naming probe: host with an app literally named `readiness-dead-port` → inject throws fail-closed. Quick to add — the appRegistrations check. Include as probe 4.\n\nLet me write the script.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"GMICloud","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cdb5a58b-f1c0-4dee-9493-e77a27dbfa08","uuid":"8543ebf4-5a8f-4af3-953c-b981762d80e2","timestamp":"2026-09-01T20:31:40.106Z","request_id":"gen-1788294525-PxBeUk8tsyUYnojzmv6Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788294525-PxBeUk8tsyUYnojzmv6Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The template has exactly one `return apps;` and `getResourceEndpoint` is defined in the module body. One critical observation: fixture/host blocks each live in their **own `if` block scope**, so the issue's \"duplicate `const` = SyntaxError\" mechanism claim needs empirical testing — if sibling-scope duplicates are legal, the RED compile check never ran (the duplicate assertion short-circuited first). I'll test both the pre-fix module's parseability and the post-fix behavior:","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"GMICloud","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cdb5a58b-f1c0-4dee-9493-e77a27dbfa08","uuid":"4f98b831-e956-4cb0-b363-7b2d65c58e93","timestamp":"2026-09-01T20:32:37.105Z","request_id":"gen-1788294525-PxBeUk8tsyUYnojzmv6Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788294525-PxBeUk8tsyUYnojzmv6Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_e53a53b195134a999259f30f","caller":{"type":"direct"},"name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/agent/projects/netscript/worktrees/007-eval-1898/.llm/tmp/eval-1898-f2/probe-fix.ts","content":"// IMPL-EVAL probe for PR #1899 — F2/F3/F4/F5/F6 over the post-fix injector.\n// Scratch evaluator tooling; not part of the repo's product or test surface.\nimport { generateRegisterApps } from \"../../packages/cli/src/kernel/templates/aspire/helpers/register/generate-register-apps.ts\";\nimport { injectReadinessFixtureApps } from \"../../packages/cli/e2e/src/application/gates/scaffold/runtime/prepare-readiness-fixture.ts\";\n\nlet failures = 0;\nfunction check(label: string, ok: boolean, detail = \"\"): void {\n  console.log(`${ok ? \"OK  \" : \"FAIL\"} ${label}${detail ? ` :: ${detail}` : \"\"}`);\n  if (!ok) failures++;\n}\nfunction assertThrowsFn(label: string, fn: () => unknown, needle: string): void {\n  try {\n    fn();\n    check(label, false, \"expected throw, none thrown\");\n  } catch (error) {\n    const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);\n    check(label, message.includes(needle), message.split(\"\\n\")[0]);\n  }\n}\n\n/** Simple (non-destructuring) const/let/var declarations — the redeclaration class. */\nfunction simpleDeclarations(source: string): string[] {\n  return [...source.matchAll(/\\b(?:const|let|var)\\s+([A-Za-z_$][\\w$]*)\\s*[=;]/gu)].map((m) => m[1]);\n}\nfunction duplicateDeclarations(source: string): string[] {\n  const all = simpleDeclarations(source);\n  return [...new Set(all.filter((n, i) => all.indexOf(n) !== i))];\n}\n/** F3: every referenced readiness_fixture_* identifier must also be declared. */\nfunction danglingFixtureReferences(source: string): string[] {\n  const declared = new Set(\n    [...source.matchAll(/\\bconst\\s+(readiness_fixture_[\\w$]*)/gu)].map((m) => m[1]),\n  );\n  const referenced = new Set<string>();\n  for (const m of source.matchAll(/(?<![\\w$])(readiness_fixture_[\\w$]*)/gu)) {\n    // Skip the declaration position itself.\n    const before = source.slice(Math.max(0, (m.index ?? 0) - 7), m.index);\n    if (/const\\s$/.test(before)) continue;\n    referenced.add(m[1]);\n  }\n  return [...referenced].filter((name) => !declared.has(name));\n}\n\nconst FIXTURE_TOKENS = [\"readiness_fixture\", \"readiness-dead-port\", \"listener-fault-controller\"];\n/** F5 host integrity: dropping injected lines must reconstruct the host byte-for-byte. */\nfunction hostLinesPreserved(host: string, injected: string): { ok: boolean; detail: string } {\n  const keptHost = host.split(\"\\n\").filter((line) =>\n    !FIXTURE_TOKENS.some((token) => line.includes(token))\n  );\n  const keptInjected = injected.split(\"\\n\").filter((line) =>\n    !FIXTURE_TOKENS.some((token) => line.includes(token))\n  );\n  return {\n    ok: keptHost.join(\"\\n\") === keptInjected.join(\"\\n\"),\n    detail: keptHost.length === keptInjected.length\n      ? \"line counts match\"\n      : `host kept ${keptHost.length} lines vs injected kept ${keptInjected.length}`,\n  };\n}\n\nasync function denoCheck(source: string, extraResource = false): Promise<{ code: number; log: string }> {\n  const root = await Deno.makeTempDir({ prefix: \"eval1898-probe-\" });\n  try {\n    const helpers = `${root}/aspire/.helpers`;\n    const modules = `${root}/aspire/.aspire/modules`;\n    await Deno.mkdir(helpers, { recursive: true });\n    await Deno.mkdir(modules, { recursive: true });\n    await Deno.writeTextFile(`${helpers}/register-apps.mts`, source);\n    await Deno.writeTextFile(\n      `${modules}/aspire.mts`,\n      `export interface ExecutableResource {\n  withEnvironment(key: string, value: string): Promise<void>;\n  withOtlpExporter(options: { protocol: string }): Promise<void>;\n  withHttpEndpoint(options: unknown): Promise<void>;\n  withBrowserLogs(): Promise<void>;\n  withHttpHealthCheck(options: unknown): Promise<void>;\n  waitForCompletion(other: ExecutableResource): Promise<void>;\n}\nexport interface DistributedApplicationBuilder {\n  addExecutable(name: string, command: string, workdir: string, args: string[]): ExecutableResource;\n}\nexport const OtlpProtocol = { HttpProtobuf: 'http-protobuf' } as const;\n`,\n    );\n    await Deno.writeTextFile(\n      `${helpers}/_aspire-compat.mts`,\n      `import type { ExecutableResource } from '../.aspire/modules/aspire.mts';\nexport interface NetScriptConfig {\n  Apps: Record<string, { Enabled?: boolean }>;\n  Version: string;\n}\nexport function buildOtelEnvVars(\n  _name: string,\n  _version: string,\n  _kind: string,\n): Record<string, string> {\n  return {};\n}\nexport function buildViteEnvVarName(_name: string): { full: string; shorthand: string } {\n  return { full: '', shorthand: '' };\n}\nexport function resolveWorkspacePath(_root: string, path: string): string {\n  return path;\n}\nexport async function withCacheReference(\n  _resource: ExecutableResource,\n  _cache: unknown,\n): Promise<void> {}\n`,\n    );\n    await Deno.writeTextFile(\n      `${helpers}/register-infrastructure.mts`,\n      'export interface InfrastructureContext { readonly primaryCacheWiring?: unknown; }\\n',\n    );\n    const output = await new Deno.Command(Deno.execPath(), {\n      args: [\"check\", \"--no-config\", `${helpers}/register-apps.mts`],\n      stdout: \"piped\",\n      stderr: \"piped\",\n    }).output();\n    return {\n      code: output.code,\n      log: new TextDecoder().decode(output.stderr) || new TextDecoder().decode(output.stdout),\n    };\n  } finally {\n    await Deno.remove(root, { recursive: true });\n  }\n}\n\n// --- Host A: three diverse apps (app + task + desktop), real generator, multiple derived ids ---\nconst hostA = generateRegisterApps({\n  apps: {\n    api: {\n      Enabled: true,\n      Runtime: \"deno\",\n      Type: \"app\",\n      Workdir: \"apps/api\",\n      TaskName: \"start\",\n      ServiceReferences: [\"worker\"],\n      WatchMode: false,\n      RequiresKv: false,\n    },\n    worker: {\n      Enabled: true,\n      Runtime: \"deno\",\n      Type: \"task\",\n      Workdir: \"apps/worker\",\n      TaskName: \"start\",\n      WatchMode: false,\n      RequiresKv: true,\n    },\n    shell: {\n      Enabled: true,\n      Runtime: \"deno\",\n      Type: \"desktop\",\n      Workdir: \"apps/shell\",\n      Prebuild: \"build\",\n      TaskName: \"start\",\n      WatchMode: false,\n      RequiresKv: false,\n    },\n  },\n  version: \"e2e\",\n  denoDefaults: { Permissions: [], WatchMode: false },\n});\nconsole.log(\"=== Host A: app+task+desktop (3 apps) ===\");\ncheck(\n  \"A0 host declares app_0/app_1/app_2 (+derived _workdir/_otel/_build)\",\n  hostA.includes(\"const app_0 \") && hostA.includes(\"const app_1 \") &&\n    hostA.includes(\"const app_2 \") && hostA.includes(\"const app_2_build \"),\n);\nconst injectedA = injectReadinessFixtureApps(hostA);\ncheck(\"A1 zero duplicate const/let/var declarations of ANY name\", duplicateDeclarations(injectedA).length === 0, `dups=${JSON.stringify(duplicateDeclarations(injectedA))}`);\ncheck(\"A2 no dangling readiness_fixture_* reference\", danglingFixtureReferences(injectedA).length === 0, `dangling=${JSON.stringify(danglingFixtureReferences(injectedA))}`);\ncheck(\"A3 registration readiness-dead-port → readiness_fixture_app_0\", injectedA.includes('apps.set(\"readiness-dead-port\", readiness_fixture_app_0);'));\ncheck(\"A4 registration listener-fault-controller → readiness_fixture_app_1\", injectedA.includes('apps.set(\"listener-fault-controller\", readiness_fixture_app_1);'));\ncheck(\"A5 host registrations intact\", injectedA.includes('apps.set(\"api\", app_0);') && injectedA.includes('apps.set(\"worker\", app_1);') && injectedA.includes('apps.set(\"shell\", app_2);'));\nconst integrityA = hostLinesPreserved(hostA, injectedA);\ncheck(\"A6 host lines byte-identical (fixture tokens filtered)\", integrityA.ok, integrityA.detail);\nassertThrowsFn(\n  \"A7 re-injecting raw injected output throws (fail-closed)\",\n  () => injectReadinessFixtureApps(injectedA),\n  \"readiness-dead-port fixture was already registered\",\n);\nassertThrowsFn(\n  \"A8 re-injecting without controller still throws (fail-closed)\",\n  () => injectReadinessFixtureApps(injectedA, false),\n  \"readiness-dead-port fixture was already registered\",\n);\nconst checkA = await denoCheck(injectedA);\ncheck(\"A9 emitted module passes deno check (parse + type)\", checkA.code === 0, checkA.log.slice(0, 600));\n\n// --- Host B: eleven task apps → host declares app_0..app_10 (two-digit boundary) ---\nconst appsB: Record<string, Record<string, unknown>> = {};\nfor (let i = 0; i < 11; i++) {\n  appsB[`svc${i}`] = {\n    Enabled: true,\n    Runtime: \"deno\",\n    Type: \"task\",\n    Workdir: `apps/svc${i}`,\n    TaskName: \"start\",\n    WatchMode: false,\n    RequiresKv: false,\n  };\n}\nconst hostB = generateRegisterApps({ apps: appsB as never, version: \"e2e\", denoDefaults: { Permissions: [], WatchMode: false } });\nconsole.log(\"=== Host B: 11 task apps (host app_0..app_10) ===\");\ncheck(\"B0 host declares two-digit app_10\", hostB.includes(\"const app_10 \"));\nconst injectedB = injectReadinessFixtureApps(hostB);\ncheck(\"B1 zero duplicate const/let/var declarations of ANY name\", duplicateDeclarations(injectedB).length === 0, `dups=${JSON.stringify(duplicateDeclarations(injectedB))}`);\ncheck(\"B2 no dangling readiness_fixture_* reference\", danglingFixtureReferences(injectedB).length === 0);\ncheck(\"B3 both fixture registrations bound to renamed ids\", injectedB.includes('apps.set(\"readiness-dead-port\", readiness_fixture_app_0);') && injectedB.includes('apps.set(\"listener-fault-controller\", readiness_fixture_app_1);'));\nconst integrityB = hostLinesPreserved(hostB, injectedB);\ncheck(\"B4 host lines byte-identical\", integrityB.ok, integrityB.detail);\nconst checkB = await denoCheck(injectedB);\ncheck(\"B5 emitted module passes deno check\", checkB.code === 0, checkB.log.slice(0, 600));\n\n// --- Host C: an app literally named readiness-dead-port must fail closed ---\nconsole.log(\"=== Host C: adversarial host app named readiness-dead-port ===\");\nconst hostC = generateRegisterApps({\n  apps: {\n    \"readiness-dead-port\": { Enabled: true, Runtime: \"deno\", Type: \"task\", Workdir: \"apps/x\", TaskName: \"start\", WatchMode: false, RequiresKv: false },\n    other: { Enabled: true, Runtime: \"deno\", Type: \"task\", Workdir: \"apps/y\", TaskName: \"start\", WatchMode: false, RequiresKv: false },\n  },\n  version: \"e2e\",\n  denoDefaults: { Permissions: [], WatchMode: false },\n});\nassertThrowsFn(\"C1 injection into colliding-name host throws\", () => injectReadinessFixtureApps(hostC), \"readiness-dead-port fixture was already registered\");\n\n// --- Host D: zero-app host (still must inject + parse) ---\nconsole.log(\"=== Host D: zero-app host ===\");\nconst hostD = generateRegisterApps({ apps: {}, version: \"e2e\", denoDefaults: { Permissions: [], WatchMode: false } });\nconst injectedD = injectReadinessFixtureApps(hostD);\ncheck(\"D1 zero duplicate declarations\", duplicateDeclarations(injectedD).length === 0, `dups=${JSON.stringify(duplicateDeclarations(injectedD))}`);\ncheck(\"D2 no dangling fixture reference\", danglingFixtureReferences(injectedD).length === 0);\nconst checkD = await denoCheck(injectedD);\ncheck(\"D3 emitted module passes deno check\", checkD.code === 0, checkD.log.slice(0, 600));\n\nconsole.log(failures === 0 ? \"\\nALL PROBE CHECKS PASSED\" : `\\n${failures} PROBE CHECK(S) FAILED`);\nDeno.exit(failures === 0 ? 0 : 1);\n"}}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference